# Build context for `docker build ... $AT_DIR`: build_test (Dockerfile-test) in
# scripts/build-docker.sh. Dockerfile-test copies only tests/, tox.ini,
# requirements.txt, tests_require.txt and MANIFEST.in, but the context root is
# this directory -- which also holds .venv (~1.2G), .tox (~97M) and
# rust/target (~337M). The repo-root .dockerignore does not apply here.
# A `#` comment must own its whole line; trailing text is part of the pattern.

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.tox/
**/.venv/
**/.rustup/
**/node_modules/
**/.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
**/rust/target/
